  Return 2.7% a year, volatility 0.8%, Sharpe ratio 3.19, worst fall −1.3%. Held
  from the start and rebalanced quarterly, without trading costs. In sample, so
  it flatters the weights: a backtest tests them on returns they had not seen.

How the weights were found
──────────────────────────
  Method     Minimum variance: the weights with the smallest variance.
  Data       US Equity, Intl Equity, Bonds, T-Bills, Gold and Real Estate.
             Monthly returns, Nov 1996 to Oct 2026.
  Estimates  Historical mean expected returns and the Ledoit–Wolf covariance,
             annualised by 12.
  Limits     Fully invested and long only.
  Solver     Interior point, optimal after 11 iterations.

